<title>UK: Sainsbury slips after broker downgrade.</title>
<headline>Sainsbury slips after broker downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in supermarket chain Sainsbury Plc eased on Thursday after NatWest Securities downgraded the stock to &quot;reduce&quot; from &quot;trading sell&quot;, market sources said.</p>
<p>In early trading, the shares were 3-1/2p lower at 360-1/2p.</p>
<p>The brokerage also cut profit forecasts for Sainsbury to 725 from 750 million stg for 1996/97, to 794 from 828 million stg for 1997/98 and to 845 from 900 million stg for 1998/99.</p>
<p>NatWest analysts were not available for comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
